						type       	"String"
						quidu      	"40E534EE0080"
						exportControl 	"Public")
					    (object ClassAttribute "amrRouter"
						quid       	"427FD63302CE"
						documentation 	
|The communication ID number (e.g. port number, serial number, data collector ID, etc.) of the parent device associated to this AMR module.
|
|Note: The thought here is that if someone swaps out a meter, they may inadvertently disrupt the AMR system. Some technologies route readings from nearby meters through a common collection point on an electricity meter. Removal of such a meter disrupts AMR for numerous nearby meters. 
						
						type       	"String"
						quidu      	"40E534EE0080"
						exportControl 	"Public")
					    (object ClassAttribute "oneWay"
						quid       	"427FD6810271"
						documentation 	"This field is set to TRUE indicate if the AMR module can only send, but can not receive messages."
						type       	"Boolean"
						quidu      	"39FE8FDF00FD"
						initv      	"1"
						exportControl 	"Public")
					    (object ClassAttribute "disconnect"
						quid       	"427FD6BE00EA"
						documentation 	"TRUE when the hardware is present to support remote whole-house disconnect capability using the AMR system."
