			    (object Class "Interval"
				quid       	"4106D97200B7"
				documentation 	
|An interval defines a time period that occurs on a periodic basis.  This is used, for example, to configure Interval Meters.  An interval meter supports multiple intervals, providing separate measurements for each one.  Different rates may apply for each interval.
|Note that the "Interval" class is intended to govern the internal behavior of the object it is associated with.  The time at which something is to be done to the object, for example the reading of an interval meter, is to be accomplished through a "ScheduledEvent."
				
				superclasses 	(list inheritance_relationship_list
				    (object Inheritance_Relationship
					quid       	"4106E2CD02AF"
					supplier   	"Logical View::61970::Core::IdentifiedObject"
					quidu      	"39DD7D18015D"))
				class_attributes 	(list class_attribute_list
				    (object ClassAttribute "length"
					quid       	"4106D9C00235"
					documentation 	
|The time interval specified in seconds.  A device like a meter may have multiple interval resolutions (e.g., 1, 5, 15, 30, or 60 minutes).
|
					
					type       	"Seconds"
					quidu      	"350376AE02A9"
					exportControl 	"Public")
				    (object ClassAttribute "offset"
					quid       	"4106D9FE03E3"
					documentation 	
|The offset from midnight (i.e., 0 hours, 0 minutes, 0 seconds) for the interval to begin.
|
					
					type       	"Seconds"
					quidu      	"350376AE02A9"
					exportControl 	"Public")
				    (object ClassAttribute "intervalCode"
					quid       	"4106DA230007"
					documentation 	"Code for this interval type."
					type       	"String"
					quidu      	"40E534EE0080"
					exportControl 	"Public")))
			    (object Class "SubcribePowerCurve"
				quid       	"441930450157"
				documentation 	"Price curve for specifying the cost of energy (X) at points in time (y1) according to a prcing structure, which is based on a tariff."
				superclasses 	(list inheritance_relationship_list
				    (object Inheritance_Relationship
					quid       	"44193163032C"
					supplier   	"Logical View::61970::Core::Curve"
					quidu      	"35157A060078")))
			    (object Class "ServiceGuarantee"
				quid       	"44215BBC0271"
				documentation 	
|A service guarantee, often imposed by a by a regulator, defines conditions that, if not satisfied, will result in the utility making a monetary payment to the customer.  Note that guarantee's identifier is in the .name attribute and the status of the guarantee is in the .subjectStatus attribute.
|
|Example Service Requirements include:
|1) If power is not restored within 24 hours, customers can claim $50 for residential customers or $100 for commercial and industrial  customers.  In addition for each extra period of 12 hours the customer's supply has not been activated, the customer can claim $25
|2) If a customer has a question about their electricity bill, the utility will investigate and respond to the inquiry within 15 working days.  If utility fails to meet its guarantee, utility will automatically pay the customer $50.
				
				superclasses 	(list inheritance_relationship_list
				    (object Inheritance_Relationship
					quid       	"44215E450128"
					supplier   	"Logical View::61968::Documentation::DocumentInheritance::Document"
					quidu      	"3AA80681005A"))
				class_attributes 	(list class_attribute_list
				    (object ClassAttribute "serviceRequirement"
					quid       	"44215C730203"
					documentation 	"Explanation of the requirement and conditions for satisfying it."
					type       	"String"
					quidu      	"40E534EE0080"
					exportControl 	"Public")
				    (object ClassAttribute "payAmount"
					quid       	"44215D6102BF"
					documentation 	"The amount to be paid by the service provider to the customer for each vilations of the Service Requirement."
					type       	"Money"
					quidu      	"350C644500EB"
					exportControl 	"Public")
				    (object ClassAttribute "automaticPay"
					quid       	"44215F9B0222"
					documentation 	"True if utility must autmatically pay the specified amount whenver the condition is not satisified.  Otherwise, customer must make a claim to receive payment."
					type       	"Boolean"
					quidu      	"39FE8FDF00FD"
					initv      	"0"
					exportControl 	"Public")
				    (object ClassAttribute "startDate"
					quid       	"442161030196"
					documentation 	"The beginning of the period in which this service guantee applies."
					type       	"AbsoluteDateTime"
					quidu      	"35036D32004F"
					exportControl 	"Public")
				    (object ClassAttribute "endDate"
					quid       	"44216156004E"
					documentation 	"The end of the period in which this service guantee applies."
					type       	"AbsoluteDateTime"
					quidu      	"35036D32004F"
					exportControl 	"Public")))
			    (object Class "PhaseLoad"
				quid       	"45080DAE0271"
				documentation 	"The class PhaseLoad models load with the unified characteristics. It can be one phase of a multi-phase load and also can be a three-phase load with unified characteristics. The aggregate relationship between DistributionLoad and PhaseLoad allows a distribution load to have any type configuration like single phase, two-phase or three-phase"
