				logical_models 	(list unit_reference_list
				    (object Class "OperationalRestriction"
					quid       	"3AA805990212"
					documentation 	
|An Operational Restriction is a type of document that can be associated with a device to describe any sort of restrictions compared with the original manufacturer's specification e.g. temporary maximum loadings, maximum switching current, do not operate if bus couplers are open etc etc. 
|In the UK, for example, if a breaker or switch ever mal-operates, this is reported centrally and utilities use their asset systems to identify all the installed devices of the same manufacturer's type. They then apply operational restrictions in the operational systems to warn operators of potential problems. After appropriate inspection and maintenance, the operational restrictions may be removed.
|
					
					superclasses 	(list inheritance_relationship_list
					    (object Inheritance_Relationship
						quid       	"3B9CD4E102F8"
						supplier   	"Logical View::61968::Documentation::DocumentInheritance::Document"
						quidu      	"3AA80681005A"))
					class_attributes 	(list class_attribute_list
					    (object ClassAttribute "startDateTime"
						quid       	"3AA8059902B2"
						documentation 	" Date and time restriction is applied."
						type       	"AbsoluteDateTime"
						quidu      	"35036D32004F"
						exportControl 	"Public")
					    (object ClassAttribute "endDateTime"
						quid       	"3AA8059A0014"
						documentation 	" Date and time restriction is lifted."
						type       	"AbsoluteDateTime"
						quidu      	"35036D32004F"
						exportControl 	"Public")
					    (object ClassAttribute "restriction"
						quid       	"3AA8059A015E"
						documentation 	" Description of restriction."
						type       	"String"
						quidu      	"40E534EE0080"
						exportControl 	"Public")
					    (object ClassAttribute "reason"
						quid       	"3AA8059A02A8"
						documentation 	" Reason for applying restriction."
						type       	"String"
						quidu      	"40E534EE0080"
						exportControl 	"Public")))
				    (object Class "SafetyDocument"
					quid       	"3AA805A2035C"
					documentation 	
| A safety document is used during the course of work on the electrical system for safety purposes. There are many types of safety documents that could be defined based upon organisational practices.
|Note: ClearanceTag is a special case of a Safety Document.
					
					superclasses 	(list inheritance_relationship_list
					    (object Inheritance_Relationship
						quid       	"3B9CD4F40064"
						supplier   	"Logical View::61968::Documentation::DocumentInheritance::Document"
						quidu      	"3AA80681005A")))
				    (object Class "ScheduleStep"
					quid       	"3AA805A3008C"
					documentation 	
| A single step within a SwitchingSchedule. Could be a switching operation, applying a network alteration or issuing a safety document.
|
|Note: Inherited name from Naming.name is used to hold Sequence Number. 
					
					superclasses 	(list inheritance_relationship_list
					    (object Inheritance_Relationship
						quid       	"3D223F1A00EA"
						supplier   	"Logical View::61970::Core::IdentifiedObject"
						quidu      	"39DD7D18015D"))
					class_attributes 	(list class_attribute_list
					    (object ClassAttribute "requiredControlAction"
						quid       	"3AA805A3012C"
						documentation 	" Control actions required to perform this step."
						type       	"String"
						quidu      	"40E534EE0080"
						exportControl 	"Public")
					    (object ClassAttribute "instructedDateTime"
						quid       	"3AA805A4026C"
						documentation 	"The time and date that the Required Control Action was issued."
						type       	"AbsoluteDateTime"
						quidu      	"35036D32004F"
						exportControl 	"Public")
					    (object ClassAttribute "completedDateTime"
						quid       	"3AA805A403B6"
						documentation 	"The time and date that the Required Control Action was completed."
						type       	"AbsoluteDateTime"
						quidu      	"35036D32004F"
						exportControl 	"Public")
					    (object ClassAttribute "status"
						quid       	"3AA805A50118"
						documentation 	"Status of this schedule step.  "
						type       	"String"
						quidu      	"40E534EE0080"
						exportControl 	"Public")
					    (object ClassAttribute "text"
						quid       	"3AA805A50262"
						documentation 	"Information regarding this switching schedule step."
						type       	"String"
						quidu      	"40E534EE0080"
						exportControl 	"Public")
					    (object ClassAttribute "desiredEndState"
						quid       	"410570E103B4"
						documentation 	"Desired end state for the associated PowerSystemResource as a result of this schedule step."
						type       	"String"
						quidu      	"40E534EE0080"
						exportControl 	"Public")))
				    (object Class "SwitchingSchedule"
					quid       	"3AA805A503DE"
					documentation 	
|A switching schedule is a document which identifies a sequence of switching operations which are to be performed on the electrical distribution network.  For example, a set of steps to isolate an item of plant with regard to safety, equipment ratings, and standards of customer service.
|Note 1:  that this (IEC 61968) SwitchingSchedule is intended to describe the full operational details for switching for real time operation which includes other operations such as grounding, applying safety documents etc. 
|Note 2: The association to ErpContact suits the UK practice of quoting specific names (e.g the crew foreman). The association to Crew is for US practice.
					
					superclasses 	(list inheritance_relationship_list
					    (object Inheritance_Relationship
						quid       	"3B9CD4E701D6"
						supplier   	"Logical View::61968::Documentation::DocumentInheritance::Document"
						quidu      	"3AA80681005A"))
					class_attributes 	(list class_attribute_list
					    (object ClassAttribute "startDateTime"
						quid       	"3AA805A600A0"
						documentation 	" Start time of switching."
						type       	"AbsoluteDateTime"
						quidu      	"35036D32004F"
						exportControl 	"Public")
					    (object ClassAttribute "endDateTime"
						quid       	"3AA805A601EA"
						documentation 	" Completion time of switching."
						type       	"AbsoluteDateTime"
						quidu      	"35036D32004F"
						exportControl 	"Public")
					    (object ClassAttribute "reason"
						quid       	"3AA805A60334"
						documentation 	" Reason for switching."
						type       	"String"
						quidu      	"40E534EE0080"
						exportControl 	"Public")))
